## 7. Instruction checklist

- [ ] Clear problem + measurable success criteria
- [ ] Solvable from instruction + repo
- [ ] No hidden tests / verifier internals / solution leak
- [ ] Not LLM-sounding / not overly prescriptive
- [ ] Matches PR scope (expand only when naturally anchored)
- [ ] Byte-identical to `environment/problem_statement.md`

---

## 8. Test checklist

- [ ] Every instruction requirement tested
- [ ] Every assertion specified or reasonably implied
- [ ] ≥10 meaningful f2p (exactly 10 meets minimum; “more than 10” needs ≥11)
- [ ] Original-failure regression present
- [ ] No p2p mutation; new f2p via `tests.patch`
- [ ] No filler / silent skip / fail-open / existence-only / agent-controlled coverage
- [ ] Count ≠ semantic proof — expert review still required

---

## 9. Oracle checklist

- [ ] `solve.sh` + `golden.patch` implement instruction
- [ ] No unrelated changes / fixture hardcoding / hidden goldens
- [ ] Offline; timeouts set; randomness controlled

---

## 10. Environment and Git checklist

- [ ] CPUs 2|4; memory 2048–16384; storage 5120–10240; gpus 0
- [ ] Timeouts: build ≤1800; agent ≤7200; verifier ≤1800
- [ ] Corrected current Fixable: Harbor network blocks required (`env=public`, `agent=allowlist`+`api.portkey.ai`, `verifier=no-network`); strip compose `network_mode="none"`; keep Dockerfile offline
- [ ] Concrete non-`latest` base image
- [ ] HEAD resolves; matches `base_commit_sha`; no remotes; clean tree; no reflog leak; `.git` <100MB
- [ ] `tests.patch` applies to intended base

---

## 11. Validation-by-role table

| Role | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| Valid-as-is submitter | Local offline Docker + Oracle 1.0 + NOP 0.0 required when technically available; Git + packaging required |
| Fixable submitter | Local strongly recommended; platform eval required before final submit; failed local check blocks ready claim; not-run must be stated |
| Reviewer | Local optional; targeted disposable checks OK; read-only |

Never claim pass without execution or reliable supplied logs.

---

## 12. Packaging checklist

- [ ] Original ZIP preserved
- [ ] Flat contents (no outer `task/`, no `runs/`)
- [ ] No reports/session/backups/caches/editor junk
- [ ] Fixable only after `ready_to_package` + preflight
- [ ] Fixable upload ZIP at `work/task ready_to_submit/<task>__corrected.zip` (cite this path)
- [ ] Valid-as-is: no new ZIP
- [ ] Invalid: evidence ZIP only, labelled manual-review

---

## 13. Common platform fields

Always: difficulty paragraph · senior estimate (`<10` / `10-20` / `20-40` / `40+`) · reviewer comments · initial review time · entire submission time. Never invent times; else `User confirmation required`.

**Snorkel voice:** narrative answers = human paragraphs (not LLM/audit tone). Difficulty, Comments, Internal reason, issue write-ups included.

**Files Changed (Fixable):** every edited path with what + why; human EC voice; skip validation rehash. Valid-as-is / no edits: `None`.

---

## 14. Legacy compatibility summary

Use current Ultra as default. Read legacy artifacts for context. Do not treat missing optional legacy files as defects. Never mix old Valid/Invalid or Accept/Reject-only systems with Ultra forms unless explicitly requested.

---

## 15. Recurring Fixable traps (see Operational Patterns for detail)

- `tests.patch`: require `git apply --check` (patch-only ≠ rename-safe)
- `allow_extra_failures`: ungraded patch tests can fail while reward=1.0
- Exactly 10 f2p ≠ live “more than 10” (≥11)
- Corrected current: ensure Harbor network blocks (+ compose cleanup); ensure `grade.py` + `golden.patch`
- Always `--task-name` + absolute paths when multiple sessions

